      "message": "fix(app): refuse a drill hole deeper than the flute from the stock surface, prove the holder clear\n\nEvery drilling op now refuses by name a hole whose depth from the stock\nsurface exceeds the tool's usable flute length - past the flutes the\nshank feeds into uncut stock, a collision. Cross holes are measured from\nthe mouths cross_stock moved out to the raw surface (#77); axial holes\nfrom the highest material (part, plus the setup stock clipped to the R\nplane) over the drill's disk down to each cycle's bottom.\n\nThe holder (holder_d / holder_len, its face flute_len + shank_len behind\nthe tip) is proven clear of the stock: axially, its face stays above the\nmaterial over its disk; on the cross drill, on every move, either its\nlower edge rides above the stock's Z top or its swept footprint stays\noutside the stock radius - so a holder that would sweep the end face on\nthe opposite-station swing is refused by name (the swing is not raised).\n\nNew logic lives in operation/drill_reach.rs. Fixtures that drilled past\na 12 mm jobber flute (real reach collisions under the rule) take a\nlong-series flute; the M1.6 deep-hole \"warns and still generates\" test\nbecomes \"is refused by name\", and posting's warned-path test moves to a\nshank-hit contour.\n\nFixes #84\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
