      "message": "fix(app): drill reach review fixes - bore/tap shank fit, per-Z-band holder, wider-body cross reach\n\nReview findings on PR #90:\n- Tap, Bore and BackBore run in an existing hole: no longer held to the\n  flute; past the flute the shank must fit the hole's diameter (refused\n  by name otherwise), the holder law kept.\n- The cross holder is judged per Z band: each move's holder Z extent\n  against the widest part/stock radius inside that band (facets clipped\n  to it), replacing the global stock radius and Z-top skip - a far\n  flange on a stepped shaft no longer refuses a hole in a slim section.\n- An off-centre cross hole's reach is measured from where the wider of\n  drill and shank meets the raw bar (to_raw_mouths returns the extra);\n  the mouth stays at the drill's edge.\n- A non-finite or negative holder_d/holder_len is refused by name, not\n  read as \"no holder\"; 0 still means no holder.\n- meets_disk skips facets with no 3D area and reads walls by their\n  edges only; drill_reach unit tests move to drill_reach_tests.rs.\n- cross_support / RECOMMENDED.md: the raw box face depth is 38 mm (47\n  is the corner radius, #85); review-fixes note on the #84 entry.\n\nTests: drill_reach (+2), new drill_reach_fit (3), drill_reach unit (+3).\n\nRefs #84\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
